MANAGED BY ANSIBLE - do not edit AdGuardHome.yaml on this host.

Source of truth:  home-config/ansible/roles/adguard/
  values           defaults/main.yml
  file layout      templates/AdGuardHome.yaml.j2
  container spec   templates/docker-compose.yml.j2

Apply:  ansible-playbook playbooks/site.yml --limit pi3-adguard --check --diff
        ansible-playbook playbooks/site.yml --limit pi3-adguard

Anything you change here, or in the AdGuard web UI, is reverted on the next
converge. The one exception is the admin password: the role reads the existing
`users:` block off this host and writes it straight back, so changing the
password in the UI is safe and persists. It is deliberately not stored in git.

This file exists because AdGuard rewrites AdGuardHome.yaml with its own YAML
emitter on every start, and that emitter strips comments - so the warning above
cannot live in the config file itself without making the role report a change,
and restart AdGuard, on every single run.
